    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **70 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors** \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `riskFlag` field so the application satisfies the spec: *return `riskFlag` true when the owner is a possible duplicate, the email domain is disposable-adjacent, or the city is over its soft capacity; otherwise false.*\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `riskFlag` boolean property to the Owner DTO schema (which regenerates `OwnerDto` with the new field), documenting the three trigger conditions.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added:\n   - A `@Mapping(target = \"riskFlag\", expression = \"java(riskFlag(owner))\")` on `toOwnerDto`.\n   - `riskFlag(Owner)` \u2014 OR of the three conditions:\n     - **possible duplicate** \u2192 `owner.getPossibleDuplicate()` (the persisted soft-match flag from the existing duplicate-detection rule).\n     - **city over soft capacity** \u2192 `owner.getCapacityWarning()` (the existing per-city warning flag, set when the city already held \u226540 owners \u2014 the soft cap below the hard limit of 50).\n     - **disposable-adjacent email** \u2192 `emailDomainDisposableAdjacent(Owner)`.\n   - `emailDomainDisposableAdjacent(Owner)` + a `DISPOSABLE_ADJACENT_TOKENS` set \u2014 flags email domains that resemble throwaway/disposable providers (e.g. `mailinator.net`, `throwaway-inbox.io`) without being on the hard blocklist, which is already rejected outright at create time.\n\nThe derivation reads only persisted owner state (`possibleDuplicate`, `capacityWarning`, `email`), so `riskFlag` is stable across the create response and subsequent `GET` reads. The new `Cp58` acceptance test (normal owner \u2192 `riskFlag` false) passes, along with all 69 pre-existing tests.\n\nNote on the design choice: the spec's \"disposable-adjacent\" was a new, undefined term (distinct from the existing hard disposable blocklist), and the only new test exercises the false case. I chose a reasonable, self-contained definition \u2014 domains containing known disposable-provider tokens (catching different-TLD variants and disposable signal words) \u2014 matching the phrase's intent.",
